<title>USA: American Air in pact to buy Shuttle.</title>
<headline>American Air in pact to buy Shuttle.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Airlines said Thursday it agreed to purchase Shuttle Inc., the successor to the Trump Shuttle, which is currently managed and partially owned by US Airways Group Inc.</p>
<p>American, a unit of AMR Corp, said it will purchase the stock, warrants and debt of Shuttle Inc. for an undisclosed price.</p>
<p>The former Trump Shuttle was taken over in April 1992 by a group of lenders. US Airways operates the shuttle under a management contract and holds 47 percent of the equity.</p>
</text>
